-- ERROR: `&` is integer-only. A bit pattern is not a property a `float`
-- has, and Saule never converts between the two numeric kinds implicitly —
-- so unlike Lua 5.3, an integral-valued float is rejected rather than
-- accepted. `int(x) & 1` is the way to say it.
class Main
	static fn main()
		local f: float = 6.0
		println(f & 1)
	end
end
